            microcirculation en am&eacute;lioration, surtout sur l'ulc&egrave;re du pied diab&eacute;tique.
            Mais le niveau de preuve est jug&eacute; <strong>tr&egrave;s faible</strong> au sens GRADE :
            param&egrave;tres h&eacute;t&eacute;rog&egrave;nes, effectifs r&eacute;duits. L'essai le plus
            dos&eacute;, &agrave; 126 J/cm&sup2;, ne montre aucun b&eacute;n&eacute;fice.
          {%- else -%}
            Systematic review of six randomised trials on chronic lower-limb wounds &mdash; the only paper
            on this page that keeps <strong>LEDs</strong> alone. Wound-area reduction, wound-bed quality and
            microcirculation all improved, particularly in diabetic foot ulcers. But the evidence is graded
            <strong>very low</strong> under GRADE: heterogeneous parameters, small samples. The
            highest-dose trial, at 126 J/cm&sup2;, showed no benefit at all.
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
        <p class="ln-study__ref">
          Miranda MB et al. <cite>Lasers Med Sci</cite> 2026;41(1).
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10103-026-04928-y" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="ln-study ln-reveal">
        <span class="ln-study__tag">{% if is_fr %}M&eacute;canisme{% else %}Mechanism{% endif %}</span>
        <span class="ln-grade ln-grade--mech">{% if is_fr %}Revue de m&eacute;canisme{% else %}Mechanism review{% endif %}</span>
        <h3 class="ln-study__claim">{% if is_fr %}Une cellule stress&eacute;e ne r&eacute;pond pas comme une cellule saine{% else %}A stressed cell does not respond like a healthy one{% endif %}</h3>
        <p class="ln-study__detail">
          {%- if is_fr -%}
            Revue de la signalisation redox mitochondriale, qui compl&egrave;te celle de 2016 sur deux
            points qu'elle n'aborde pas : la lumi&egrave;re produit des effets apparemment
            <strong>oppos&eacute;s</strong> selon que la cellule est saine ou stress&eacute;e, et elle peut
            agir en <strong>pr&eacute;conditionnement</strong> &mdash; avant l'effort plut&ocirc;t
            qu'apr&egrave;s. C'est l'argument m&eacute;canistique derri&egrave;re une s&eacute;ance
            <a href="{{ pre_url }}">avant l'entra&icirc;nement</a>.
          {%- else -%}
            A review of mitochondrial redox signalling, filling in two things the 2016 review does not
            cover: light produces apparently <strong>opposite</strong> effects depending on whether the cell
            is healthy or stressed, and it can act as <strong>preconditioning</strong> &mdash; before
            exercise rather than after. This is the mechanistic argument behind a
            <a href="{{ pre_url }}">pre-workout session</a>.
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
        <p class="ln-study__ref">
          Hamblin MR. <cite>Photochem Photobiol</cite> 2018;94(2):199&ndash;212.
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.1111/php.12864" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

